This is not a MIDI file. It is its name.

The real one was two minutes and thirty-one seconds of a canyon, written for
a synthesiser chip, shipped with the system, and opened by everyone exactly
once - which was enough, because thirty years later the people who opened it
once can still hum the first eight bars.

Nothing on this desktop will open it. A terminal has no wave device and no
synthesiser, and a program that opened this file and played nothing would be
a joke told once.

If you want to hear it, you already can: it is in your head.
